Title: Bound the sync client's retries
Label: kind:fix

### Objective

The sync client retries a failed push without limit. Bound the retries so a dead remote stops the push instead of looping.

### Non-goals

Changing the push protocol or its backoff curve.

### Affected interfaces/contracts

Not drafted: the authored text for this section did not pass the issue-text screen. Read the finding under Origin below.

### Acceptance

- A push against a dead remote stops after the retry bound.
- A push that succeeds on a retry still completes.

### Scope / declared paths

daemon/internal/sync/

### Dependencies

starts-after #1234: set aside during the review of #1234; the planner confirms the relationship

### Origin

Retry budget is unbounded
The client retries a failed push forever.

Location: daemon/internal/sync/push.go:40-52

Adjudication rationale: adjacent to the goal: the unit changes the push path, not its retries
